---
interface Props { compact?: boolean; }
const { compact = false } = Astro.props;
const metrics = [
  { value: '51–55', label: 'tok/s decode on real coding-agent sessions at about 70 W', note: 'Flat from 28K to 189K of context.', home: true },
  { value: '29/35', label: 'Same accuracy as stock gufo on hard reasoning problems', note: 'Bubo solved 29 and gufo 27, on a pre-release build, 2026-10-10. Decode is about 24% faster.', home: true, href: '/docs/benchmarks/#reasoning-check-halowin-bubo-and-gufo-pixmaates-windows-port' },
  { value: '25×', label: 'faster to resume a 109K-token chat after a restart', note: '3.5 s with the disk cache against 88.8 s without.', home: true },
  { value: '1,364', label: 'tok/s prefill', note: 'The NPU adds 5–7% more at 8K.' },
  { value: '96.5', label: 'tok/s on code edits', note: 'Edits that reuse your file’s text, first request.' },
  { value: '1,287', label: 'tok/s natural-text prefill', note: '32K of context.' },
  { value: '102.2', label: 'tok/s combined with 8 users at once', note: 'Plain decode, 4K of context each.' },
];
---
<div class:list={['measurements', { compact }]}>
  <p class="model-line">Measured with Huihui’s abliterated Qwen3.8 Flash Next (125B parameters, 6B active) in the UD-Q4_K_XL quant, on AMD Strix Halo. Every number comes from a 13-inch laptop at its normal plugged-in Performance setting, approximately 70 W. That is full-speed local inference at laptop power: about half of what a desktop Strix Halo draws, so less heat and fan noise than a desktop or an overclocked laptop, on a machine you can carry. <a href="/docs/system-setup/#power-mode">How to reach this power</a>. Desktops and Manual mode have more headroom: see the <a href="/docs/benchmarks/#estimated-at-140-w">140 W estimate</a>.</p>
  <dl class="benchmark-strip" aria-label="Halowin Bubo measured benchmark results">
    {(compact ? metrics.filter(m => m.home) : metrics).map(metric => (
      <div class="benchmark-tile">
        <dt>{metric.href ? <a href={metric.href}>{metric.label}</a> : metric.label}</dt>
        <dd class="benchmark-value">{metric.prefix && <span class="benchmark-prefix">{metric.prefix} </span>}{metric.value}</dd>
        <dd class="benchmark-note">{metric.note}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>
</div>
<style>
  .model-line { margin: 0 0 14px; color: var(--muted); font-size: .98rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .benchmark-strip { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-block: 1px solid var(--line); padding-block: 26px; margin: 0 0 24px; gap: 30px 24px; }
  .compact .benchmark-strip { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-top: 0; margin-top: 8px; }
  .benchmark-tile { display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-width: 0; }
  .benchmark-tile dt { order: 1; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.4; margin-top: 8px; }
  .benchmark-tile dd { margin: 0; }
  .benchmark-value { order: 0; color: var(--accent); font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 3.4vw, 3.3rem); line-height: 1.1; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; letter-spacing: -.035em; }
  .benchmark-prefix { font-size: .4em; letter-spacing: 0; margin-right: .1em; }
  .benchmark-note { order: 2; color: var(--muted); font-size: .93rem; line-height: 1.45; margin-top: 8px !important; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .compact .benchmark-strip { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .benchmark-strip { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .compact .benchmark-strip { gap: 26px 18px; } .benchmark-value { font-size: 2.5rem; } }
  @media (max-width: 350px) { .compact .benchmark-strip { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
